    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="453" ed="#liebermann"/>[5] Swa sceal god scyrman his hlafordes healdan, do ymbe his agen, swa swa he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="22.7" corresp="#wit-b">Swa sceal god scyrman his hlafor||des Healdan do ymbe his agen swa swa he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="334" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Swa sceal god scyrman his hlafordes healdan, do ymbe his agen, swa swa he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="453" ed="#liebermann"/>So soll ein guter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="p" target="#Ger_5.lnote.de1.p"/> Amtmann [das Gut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ger_5.lnote.de.1"/>] seines Herrn hüten, mag er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="q" target="#Ger_5.lnote.de1.q"/> betreffend sein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ger_5.lnote.de.2"/> eigen handeln, wie er will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">So shall a good reeve guard his lord's [estate], whatever he may do about his own as he wishes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">Thus a good shireman should maintain his lord’s estate just as he would want concerning his own.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="335" ed="#rabin-doml"/>A good shire reeve must oversee his lord’s property thus, no matter what he does about his own.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">‘mag er … handeln’: concessive, after Pogatscher. Liebermann compares Gerefa 12.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_5.lnote.de1.p" n="p" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">453</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ger_5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">253</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Interesse’ Pogatscher in <hi rend="italic">Anglia</hi> 23, 287; ‘Güter’ Sk</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘interest’ Pogatscher in <hi rend="italic">Anglia</hi> 23, 287; ‘goods’ Sk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ger_5.lnote.de1.q" n="q" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">453</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘<hi rend="italic">concessiv</hi>’; <hi rend="italic">Pogatscher</hi> Anglia 23, 287</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘<hi rend="italic">concessive</hi>’; <hi rend="italic">Pogatscher</hi> Anglia 23, 287</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ger_5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">253</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht besteht auch des Vogts Eigen z. T. in Land, das von diesem Herrschaftsgut entliehen ist, wie ja <hi rend="italic">reveland</hi> im Domesday oft vorkommt (Ellis <hi rend="italic">Introd. to Domesday</hi> I 231), und wie auch der Büttel vom Herrn mit Land ausgestattet war; Rect 18, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps the bailiff’s own property too consists in part of land lent out of this demesne, as indeed <hi rend="italic">reveland</hi> often occurs in Domesday (Ellis <hi rend="italic">Introd. to Domesday</hi> I 231), and as the beadle too was provided with land by the lord; Rect 18, 1</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
